<item>
            <title>[LU-20802] P2: OBJECT-scope read and lseek</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20802</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Summary&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Summary&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Implement OBJECT-scope direct pread and lseek (SEEK_DATA, SEEK_HOLE, SEEK_END).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Description&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Description&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Replace the P1 &lt;tt&gt;-EOPNOTSUPP&lt;/tt&gt; stub for &lt;tt&gt;OBJECT&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;OBJECT&lt;/tt&gt; is its own entry path: the caller names one OST object, and &lt;tt&gt;pos&lt;/tt&gt; is an offset on that object.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;One sub-I/O. The object offset is used as-is (identity mapping).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;No component-extent walk, and no file-offset to stripe-offset rewrite.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;O_DIRECT&lt;/tt&gt; only.&#160; &lt;tt&gt;mmap&lt;/tt&gt; is rejected.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;ios_fid&lt;/tt&gt; is the only identity, and it must be non-zero.&lt;br/&gt;
EOF is the target object&apos;s kms. This is a third EOF case, beside the file &lt;tt&gt;i_size&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;ci_parity_eof&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;OBJECT&lt;/tt&gt; does not set &lt;tt&gt;ci_parity_io&lt;/tt&gt;, so &lt;tt&gt;ci_parity_eof&lt;/tt&gt; is unchanged.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Uninstantiated component: &lt;tt&gt;-ENOENT&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Dead object: &lt;tt&gt;-EIO&lt;/tt&gt;. Do not fall back to &lt;tt&gt;CIT_EC_RD&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;write&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;truncate&lt;/tt&gt;, and &lt;tt&gt;fallocate&lt;/tt&gt; on an &lt;tt&gt;OBJECT&lt;/tt&gt;-scope fd stay &lt;tt&gt;-EOPNOTSUPP&lt;/tt&gt; until P3. File-offset helpers are left unchanged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
